ence of text chunks and return a list of lines of\n        length \'self.width\' or less.  (If \'break_long_words\' is false,\n        some lines may be longer than this.)  Chunks correspond roughly\n        to words and the whitespace between them: each chunk is\n        indivisible (modulo \'break_long_words\'), but a line break can\n        come between any two chunks.  Chunks should not have internal\n        whitespace; ie. a chunk is either all whitespace or a "word".\n        Whitespace chunks will be removed from the beginning and end of\n        lines, but apart from that whitespace is preserved.\n        ')), Assign(targets=[Name(id='lines', ctx=Store())], value=List()), If(test=Compare(left=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='width'), ops=[LtE()], comparators=[Constant(value=0)]), body=[Raise(exc=Call(func=Name(id='ValueError'), args=[BinOp(left=Constant(value='invalid width %r (must be > 0)'), op=Mod(), right=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='width'))]))]), If(test=Compare(left=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='max_lines'), ops=[IsNot()], comparators=[Constant(value=None)]), body=[If(test=Compare(left=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='max_lines'), ops=[Gt()], comparators=[Constant(value=1)]), body=[Assign(targets=[Name(id='indent', ctx=Store())], value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='subsequent_indent'))], orelse=[Assign(targets=[Name(id='indent', ctx=Store())], value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='initial_indent'))]), If(test=Compare(left=BinOp(left=Call(func=Name(id='len'), args=[Name(id='indent')]), op=Add(), right=Call(func=Name(id='len'), args=[Call(func=Attribute(value=Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='placeholder'), attr='lstrip'))])), ops=[Gt()], comparators=[Attribute(value=Name(id='self'), attr='width')]), body=[Raise(exc=Call(func=Name(id='ValueError'), args=[Constant(value='placeholder too large for max width')]))])]), Expr(value=Call(func=Attribute(value=Name(id='chunks'), attr='reverse'))), While(test=N